{% macro decisionPath() %}
<figure class="article-figure article-figure-responsive">
<div class="article-figure-desktop figure-wide figure-wide-path" role="group" aria-label="The eight steps, and the point where you stop">
<ol class="figure-wide-steps" role="list">
<li><span>Ask where the business loses money</span></li>
<li><span>Pull the real numbers</span></li>
<li><span>Sort them: facts, fair guesses, unknowns</span></li>
<li><span>Write down all five options</span></li>
<li><span>Score every option, money against proof</span></li>
<li><span>Choose, and write down why</span>
<p class="figure-wide-exit"><strong>Nothing clears the bar?</strong><span>Stop. Say so out loud.</span></p></li>
<li><span>Run one 90-day test with a stop rule</span></li>
<li><span>Ask six questions before you approve spend</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="article-figure-mobile">
<ol class="figure-flow">
<li><span>Ask where the business loses money</span></li>
<li><span>Pull the real numbers</span></li>
<li><span>Sort them: facts, fair guesses, unknowns</span></li>
<li><span>Write down all five options</span></li>
<li><span>Score every option, money against proof</span></li>
<li><span>Choose, and write down why</span>
<p class="figure-flow-exit"><strong>Nothing clears the bar?</strong> Stop. Say so out loud.</p></li>
<li><span>Run one 90-day test with a stop rule</span></li>
<li><span>Ask six questions before you approve spend</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figcaption>Two hours of work, and a real exit. Most of the method happens before anyone writes a line of code.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro leadFollowUpLeak() %}
<figure class="article-figure">
<p class="figure-eyebrow">Paid demand</p>
<div class="figure-columns figure-funnel">
<div class="figure-card"><b class="figure-card-figure">120</b><span class="figure-card-label">enquiries</span><span class="figure-card-note">in 90 days</span></div>
<div class="figure-card"><b class="figure-card-figure">64</b><span class="figure-card-label">quotes sent</span></div>
<div class="figure-gap"><strong>Follow-up leak</strong><span>from sent to chased</span></div>
<div class="figure-card is-watch"><b class="figure-card-figure">18</b><span class="figure-card-label">chased</span></div>
<div class="figure-card"><b class="figure-card-figure">11</b><span class="figure-card-label">closed</span></div>
</div>
<p class="figure-aside"><b>71</b><span>got one attempt and nothing after</span></p>
<p class="figure-summary"><strong>64 quotes sent. Only 18 chased.</strong> The demand arrived. The follow-up did not.</p>
<figcaption>Illustrative figures only: these numbers were invented to show the shape of the leak and are not from a real company.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro leadFollowUpBuyOrder() %}
<figure class="article-figure">
<p class="figure-eyebrow">Buy in this order</p>
<ol class="figure-columns">
<li class="figure-card"><span class="figure-rank">First</span><span class="figure-card-title">Fix the process</span></li>
<li class="figure-card"><span class="figure-rank">Then</span><span class="figure-card-title">Use the shared inbox or CRM</span><span class="figure-card-note">you already pay for</span></li>
<li class="figure-card"><span class="figure-rank">Then</span><span class="figure-card-title">Automate the reminders</span></li>
<li class="figure-card is-watch"><span class="figure-rank">Last</span><span class="figure-card-title">Put AI on top of that</span>
<p class="figure-callout">Most companies start here</p></li>
</ol>
<p class="figure-summary">The first three steps come before AI.</p>
<figcaption>Build from the process up. Most companies I met were shopping for AI while the first three steps were still missing.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro buildCostOwnershipCost() %}
<figure class="article-figure">
<div class="figure-burden" role="img" aria-label="A small build block sits beside a much taller ownership stack made of maintenance, breaks, security, reliability, upkeep and the risk of building the wrong thing.">
<div class="figure-burden-build"><span class="figure-burden-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span class="figure-burden-block">Build</span></div>
<div class="figure-burden-own"><span class="figure-burden-brace" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="figure-burden-stack"><span>Wrong thing</span><span>Upkeep</span><span>Reliability</span><span>Security + data</span><span>Breaks</span><span>Maintenance</span></div><strong>Ownership</strong></div>
</div>
<figcaption>The cost of building fell. The cost of owning what you built did not.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro buildBuyQuestions() %}
<figure class="article-figure">
<ol class="figure-question-map">
<li><p><span>Team + time + internal</span><strong>Build</strong></p></li>
<li><p><span>Internal or customer-facing</span><strong>Internal: name an owner. Customer-facing: use a credentialed technical team.</strong></p></li>
<li><p><span>Named owner</span><strong>No owner → no build</strong></p></li>
<li class="is-watch"><p><span>Build + upkeep + risk</span><strong>No time or team → usually buy</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<figcaption>Four questions: team and capacity, exposure, ownership, then the full resource picture.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro buildBuyRunOrder() %}
<figure class="article-figure">
<div class="figure-route" role="img" aria-label="Decision route: if nothing is broken, leave it alone. If the process is not stable and documented, fix that first. Otherwise decide whether it is worth automating, then run the build or buy questions. The outcomes are build, credentialed technical team or buy, and buy.">
<div class="figure-route-main"><span>Broken?</span><span>Stable?</span><span>Worth<br>automating?</span><span>Build<br>or buy?</span></div>
<div class="figure-route-exits"><p><b>Nothing broken</b><strong>Leave it alone</strong></p><p><b>Not stable</b><strong>Fix that first</strong></p></div>
<div class="figure-route-outcomes"><span>Build</span><span>Technical team<br>or buy</span><span>Buy</span></div>
</div>
<figcaption>This is the judgment I would bring to a specific proposal, not a universal formula.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}
